uild profile (AI-assisted review, under my direction): [profile.release] sets panic = \"abort\" but has no overflow-checks key, so, unless the build passes -C overflow-checks elsewhere, release builds wrap silently on integer overflow while debug builds panic. For size/length arithmetic derived from untrusted input (e.g. archive headers), wrapping would skip the check that panics in debug. Is this intentional? If not, enabling overflow-checks = true for release, measuring the boot-time/size cost, and adding one regression test on a wrapping size computation might be worth considering. Checked at main@fbe6472e.","closed_by":{"login":"gmkurtzer","id":13984965,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer","html_url":"https://github.com/gmkurtzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/43/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/43/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}